  "_evidence": "STRUCTURAL mapping for the AsiaMaterialsBrief legacy import (amb-launch W2, 27-10-26). No site id, no image host: those live in the owner-held overlay ~/amb-private/overlay.json. Every key in _provisional is an OWNER DECISION still open; the values are SUGGESTIONS only and --require-final (implied for any non-local run) refuses them. The old site row in public.sites is NOT known yet (guess slug asiamaterialsbrief): run 01-discover-amb.sql first. Old section values are the old site's URL slugs (briefing, materials, interiors-ffe, lighting-tech, projects, press-room, intelligence, exhibition, events-awards); old SUBSECTION values are UNKNOWN until discovery (section 3 of 01-discover-amb.sql): the old site filters with ?sub=<Name> (e.g. ?sub=Industry%20News) and sometimes ?sub=<slug> (?sub=policy-trade), so both the lower-cased design name and the new slug are mapped for every sub-section (resolveTaxonomy lower-cases the stored value), plus 'new & sustainable' / 'new-sustainable' for new-sustainable-materials. Open decisions: (1) status.map: suggestion published only, like agr; catch-up runs before cutover pick up what the old site publishes later. (2) categories.map: old subs equal to a new sub-section name or slug pass through; any other old sub keeps its pillar with NO sub-section (<pillar>/*), to be re-checked against the discovery list; press-room/* goes to press-room with no sub-section (single-home). intelligence, exhibition and events-awards have NO entry on purpose (they are pages on the new site, not pillars): unmapped is reject, so a row there stops the run until the owner picks a pillar (suggestion to discuss: intelligence -> briefing, events-awards -> briefing with tag fairs, exhibition -> skip or a later exhibitors import). projects/specified and projects/design-voices are mapped like the other subs: the engine-side block applies to new AI pieces, not to imported human ones. (3) authors: even split over the 6 staff names of the Team page (mode even, per-author counts differ by at most 1; agr moved from slugHash to even after the owner's first dry run); legacy bylines are not kept. (4) tags: only the 6 approved tags survive (D6); the renames are guesses until the discovery's top-40 tag list is read. (5) media.bodyImages: drop (default, counted) or hero-if-missing; decide after the body image count. The old image library (media_assets) goes to the content-engine Media Engine in a separate plan, not through this mapping. (6) body.reflowMaxChars: 380 is the aer/agr value (old network sites store each section as one block and split it at render time); confirm on a few old article pages after the first dry run. (7) archivedAs section (301) vs 410. (8) old origin apex https://asiamaterialsbrief.com or www; article path /article/{slug} (the old site's own pattern); /intelligence, /exhibition/*, /events-awards, /studio, /press-room-submit and the other page routes get hand-written redirects in amb-web at cutover, not from this mapping.",
